uo;2027&rdquo; and &ldquo;early 2027&rdquo; for its start</strong>, so the chart pins no date. OpenAI's &ldquo;in the coming months&rdquo; is the same wording across several reports, including <a href="https://www.unite.ai/openai-to-honor-shared-robots-txt-signal-for-ai-training-preferences/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Unite.AI</a>. <strong>One report points out that Anthropic's participation rests not on a company announcement but on the draft author's IETF mailing-list post (&ldquo;has already started implementing support&rdquo;)</strong>, so the table says only &ldquo;draft author's employer; implementation started.&rdquo; Meta was not in the four-company announcement, and no source stating its position on support was found. The AIPREF vocabulary draft (train-ai, ai-use, search), the <code>Content-Usage</code> field and the missed August target follow summaries citing the <a href="https://datatracker.ietf.org/wg/aipref/about/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">IETF AIPREF working group page</a>. The draft author is not a public figure and is not named; the document identifier is kept because readers need it to find the original. This wiki's change can be checked directly in the repository's <code>robots.txt</code> and <code>tools/build_ai_export.py</code>.</p>
